## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ability to design real-time, scalable guardrails spanning telemetry, model routing, and incident response in multi-tenant LLM gateways, a common production pain point.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming telemetry and per-tenant baselines
- Anomaly scoring combining statistical and rule-based signals
- Remediation policies: throttle, safe-model routing, quarantine
- Auditability and drift handling across tenants
- Data locality and privacy impacts

## Code Example
```javascript
function score(latency, tokens, entropy, baseline) {
  const zLat = (latency - baseline.latency.mean) / baseline.latency.std;
  const zTok = (tokens - baseline.tokens.mean) / baseline.tokens.std;
  const zEnt = (entropy - baseline.entropy.mean) / baseline.entropy.std;
  return Math.max(0, Math.abs(zLat) + Math.abs(zTok) + Math.abs(zEnt));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune thresholds to minimize false positives for bursts?
- How would you validate end-to-end remediation without impacting real users?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable, privacy-aware routing under mixed latency budgets and per-tenant policies. Requires integration of policy engines, redaction, quotas, data locality, auditability, and testing under burst traffic.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant policy modeling
- Latency budgeting and SLA targets
- Model variant routing and cost-speed tradeoffs
- Redaction at prompt and response with data locality
- Tamper-evident auditing and drift detection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing decision example
function decideRoute(ctx) {
  const tenant = ctx.tenant
  const policy = policyStore[tenant] || policyStore['default']
  // Evaluate latency and redact flags
  const model = policy.chooseModel(ctx.prompt)
  const redact = policy.shouldRedact(ctx.prompt)
  return { model, redact }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test latency budgets under burst traffic and verify cross-region consistency?
- How would you implement policy drift detection and safe rollback without service disruption?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical governance, privacy compliance, and performance in multi-tenant LLM ops, including policy versioning, KMS integration, and audit-ability under latency pressure.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant redaction policies (regex/ML)
- Tamper-evident, region-local audit logs
- KMS-backed policy keys and versioning
- Drift checks and alerting
- Latency considerations: streaming redaction

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch: redaction path
function redactPromptsAndOutputs(prompt, policy) {
  const redactedIn = applyRedaction(prompt, policy.inputRules);
  const redactedOut = applyRedaction(await llm(redactedIn), policy.outputRules);
  return { redactedIn, redactedOut };
}
```

